n text, JSON, or both."],[633,"`--format text|json|both`: Choose human text, JSON, or both."],[732,"`--format text|json|both`: Choose text, JSON, or both."],[896,"`--format text|json|both`: Choose text, JSON, or both."],[921,"`--format text|json|both`: Choose text, JSON, or both."],[948,"`--format text|json|both`: Choose text, JSON, or both."],[987,"`--format text|json|both`: Choose text, JSON, or both."],[1016,"`--format text|json|both`: Choose text, JSON, or both."],[1048,"`--format text|json|both`: Choose text, JSON, or both."],[561,"`--format text|json|both`: Choose the output form."],[437,"`--format text|json|both`: Choose the result envelope form."],[339,"`--format text|json|both`: Return a text summary, a JSON envelope, or both."],[473,"`--git-init`: Create a git repository automatically in non-interactive mode."],[625,"`--goal <goalId>`: Filter to one goal identifier."],[728,"`--input <path|->`: Provide a JSON payload with `goal`, optional `budget`, and optional `at`."],[557,"`--input <path|->`: Provide a JSON payload with `question`, `topK`, and optional `at`."],[435,"`--input <path|->`: Provide a structured JSON payload instead of flags."],[985,"`--input <path|->`: Required JSON payload describing promotion candidates."],[1046,"`--input <path|->`: Required JSON payload describing the session wrap."],[628,"`--kind <kind>`: Limit results to `session`, `artifact`, `memory`, `harness`, or `ingest`."],[472,"`--merge-existing`: Reuse existing docs as primary sources before creating draft files. This is the default behavior."],[469,"`--mode auto|empty|existing|monorepo|docs-heavy`: Override repository mode detection. Default is `auto`."],[468,"`--non-interactive`: Same intent as `--yes`, useful in scripted flows."],[474,"`--output text|json|both`: Choose the human summary, JSON summary, or both."],[525,"`--path <glob>`: Filter indexed docs by a repository-local glob."],[627,"`--session <sessionId>`: Filter to one source session identifier."],[526,"`--show-missing`: Include commits that do not have a snapshot manifest."],[629,"`--since <iso>`: Lower bound for `recordedAt`."],[433,"`--since <sha>`: Index only changes since a commit."],[470,"`--strategy minimal|balanced|full`: Control how aggressively stage-1 foundational docs are generated. Default is `balanced`."],[558,"`--top-k <n>`: Control how many hits to return."],[524,"`--type <docType>`: Filter the history to one canonical document type."],[535,"`--type` and `--path` filter snapshot content, not raw git diffs."],[781,"`--type` narrows the refresh by doc type."],[630,"`--until <iso>`: Upper bound for `recordedAt`."],[1022,"`--view default` balances readability and detail."],[737,"`--view default` preserves a balanced amount of detail."],[568,"`--view default` returns the standard readable hit projection."],[1023,"`--view full` is only for cases where the restored packet must carry richer text from retrieval hits."],[738,"`--view full` is useful only when downstream reasoning truly needs richer text."],[569,"`--view full` keeps the richest text projection and is the most expensive for context windows."],[1021,"`--view minimal` is the best default for agent resumes."],[736,"`--view minimal` is the safest default for agent context windows."],[567,"`--view minimal` returns the smallest useful hit shape."],[560,"`--view minimal|default|full`: Choose how much hit detail to project."],[523,"`--view minimal|default|full`: Choose one-line scan output, semantic blocks, or richer per-document detail."],[632,"`--view minimal|default|full`: Choose one-line scan output, structured event blocks, or richer provenance detail."],[731,"`--view minimal|default|full`: Control how much detail is projected into the packet."],[1015,"`--view minimal|default|full`: Control how much retrieved detail is projected into the packet."],[467,"`--yes`: Accept defaults and skip prompts."],[522,"`-n, --max-count <n>`: Limit the final number of emitted entries."],[631,"`-n, --max-count <n>`: Limit the final number of emitted events."],[243,"`.ragit/config.toml`"],[245,"`.ragit/guide/guide-index.json`"],[244,"`.ragit/guide/templates/*`"],[302,"`.ragit/memory/**` is the **control plane**. It stores session wraps and current working state. This area is good for resuming work, but it is not meant to be your general searchable knowledge base."],[154,"`.ragit/memory/**` is the control plane for working state and session history."],[246,"`.ragit/store/meta.json`"],[521,"`[revRange]`: Optional git revision range such as `HEAD~10..HEAD`."],[338,"`<command-path...>`: The full command path. Multi-word commands are passed as separate words, for example `memory promote` or `hooks install`."],[1014,"`<goal>`: The task you want to resume."],[688,"`<key>`: The dotted config key to update."],[689,"`<value>`: The value to store."],[484,"`actions`"],[487,"`actions` reports planned create/reuse/skip outcomes for stage-1 foundational docs."],[50,"`Architecture Decision (ADR)`"],[85,"`Architecture Decision (ADR)` vs `Plan`: `ADR` records a stable decision. `Plan` records the sequence of work to execute."],[101,"`architecture_view` is advisory only.\nRAGit still classifies documents by canonical `type`, so `SPEC`, `SRS`, `DDD`, `PBD`, and `ADR` remain the source of truth for document behavior."],[650,"`artifact review` is the quality gate between capture/materialize and promotion."],[658,"`artifact review` transitions captured artifacts into reviewed lifecycle states. It is the explicit gate before durable promotion for both session and harness artifacts."],[649,"`artifact review`: move captured artifacts into `reviewed`, `retracted`, `superseded`, or `archived`."],[485,"`bootstrap`"],[488,"`bootstrap` reports the AGENTS/guide/zvec state or planned state during `--dry-run`."],[801,"`capture` does not execute the suite. Use `harness run` for execution."],[812,"`capture` writes candidate artifacts under `.ragit/artifacts/harness/**`."],[683,"`config set` updates one key in `.ragit/config.to